olidating control over the upper-middle board.\n\n**Reason**: This move offers the highest immediate material gain among all available options by converting 4 opponent pieces. It also denies the opponent the strong move to E1, securing the D1 piece and surrounding area.\n\n**Answer**: (D,1) -> (E,1)\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: The move (D,1) -> (E,1) is the strongest option available. It is a cloning move that targets the core of the opponent's cluster, capturing 4 pieces (F1, D2, E2, F2). This results in a massive 9-point swing in the game score (Player +5, Opponent -4). Furthermore, taking control of E1 protects your piece at D1 and prevents the opponent from using E1 to counter-attack.\n\nReason: This move maximizes piece conversion (4 captures) while adding a new piece to the board (clone). It is strictly better than the jumping alternative (D,1) -> (F,3) which also captures 4 but leaves the source square empty. It also defends against the opponent's potential threat of occupying E1.\n\nAnswer: (D,1) -> (E,1)"}
